<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Regenerated 2026-09-23 from Test3/Logo 2.png. The foreground is the mark
    alone - the Q and its swoosh, cut at x=790 where the wordmark starts - at
    64% of the 108dp canvas, which keeps it inside the 66dp safe zone whatever
    mask the launcher applies. The wordmark is left out on purpose: it is
    unreadable at 48px.

    The background is brand sand, not the brown: the mark is brown, and brown
    on brown reads as a muddy blob at icon size.

    No <monochrome>: the themed-icon layer wants a flat silhouette, and pointing
    it at full-colour artwork just gets it tinted into a blob. Without one,
    Android falls back to this icon, which is the better of the two outcomes.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
